From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 19:39:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07937/11362] [outer-loop] FLIP the HUD trio ON (operator
 decision): +1 game (r11l) on EVERY seed, zero losses, zero new test failures

SUBMITTED_EDGE_BAR_HUD_MASK_ENABLED        False -> True
SUBMITTED_HUD_MASK_COLLAPSE_GUARD_ENABLED  False -> True
SUBMITTED_HUD_MASK_STAGE2_CONFIRM_ENABLED  False -> True
All three together -- _assert_hud_flag_coupling() refuses any other combination AT IMPORT.

EVIDENCE (results/experiment_5960_hud_mask_repair_full_corpus.json; 300 cells, real condition,
MATCHED-SEED against arm B2 = the current live config):
  arm            seed .724          seed .725               seed .726     verdict
  G   detector   +r11l +tn36        +ar25 +r11l +tn36       -lp85         REGRESSES
  G2  +guard     +r11l +tn36        +r11l +tn36             -lp85         REGRESSES
  G3  +Stage2    +r11l              +r11l                   +r11l         CLEAN
Only the FULLY-SAFE configuration gains on every seed while losing nothing. The safety stages are
not overhead on a working lever -- they are what MAKE it a working lever: G and G2 buy tn36/ar25 by
over-masking and pay for it with lp85. That is why the coupling is a mechanical assertion.

DETECTOR FIDELITY: verified against the reference on all 25 public games -- 1151 -> 1564 mask cells,
0 dropped (25/25), 0 extra (25/25). r11l's 64 cells are byte-identical to the oracle diagnostic while
being derived from FRAME STATISTICS ALONE (no per-game constants, no source reading, hidden-game
legal). r11l node inflation 0.9986 -> 0.201; r11l is a game the agent had NEVER won.

REGRESSION VERIFICATION -- same tree, identical artifacts, flags reverted via env (the control that
caught a masked regression on the frontier flip, where totals matched but the SETS did not):
  HUD ON  44 failed / 7633 passed     HUD OFF 50 failed / 7627 passed
  ON minus OFF = ZERO new failures. The 6 OFF-only failures are HUD guard tests now correctly
  asserting the ON default. Targeted battery 153/153.

Six guard tests updated rather than bypassed -- they existed to force a conscious, recorded decision
before a flip, which is what they did. The OFF behaviour stays a real, load-bearing property (it is
what arm B2 measures against), so it is now requested EXPLICITLY via kwargs instead of inherited from
module defaults. The coupling test still proves the property it was written for -- the detector must
never ship without BOTH safety stages -- now provoked by turning a SAFETY stage off, since the
detector alone is the legal shipped config.

HONEST LIMIT, same as the frontier flip earlier today: PUBLIC-corpus evidence via the offline dev
twin. Public games score ~0 on the hidden set, so this is a capability argument, NOT demonstrated
hidden-game transfer. The gate was full-corpus per-seed regression; r11l was the pre-registered
SIGNAL, never the gate.
NOT changed: SUBMITTED_AUTO_HUD_MASK_ENABLED (pre-existing True). Its own over-masking question is
recorded in ops/known-issues.md as a HYPOTHESIS WITH A NAMED CONFOUND -- do not cite it as proven.

